IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part6-graduated`

-- Tests for Part 6 (regulations 15 to 20, lines 147 to 273). Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Part 6`

-- A survivor whose spouse or civil partner died while they were married or civil partners of each other, who paid graduated
-- contributions; married in 2010 (before 6 April 2016); not remarried; no deferral.
GIVEN died IS A DATE
      `deceased reached` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `survivor reaches` IS A DATE
      asked IS A DATE
      remarried IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a survivor`
`a survivor` died `deceased reached` `survivor reaches` asked remarried MEANS
    `Facts about a survivor` WITH
        `the date as at which the question is asked` IS asked
        `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS TRUE
        `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS TRUE
        `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS Date 1 6 2010
        `the date the deceased died` IS died
        `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS `deceased reached`
        `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS `survivor reaches`
        `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS remarried
        `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
        `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
        `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
        `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE

§§ `Regulation 16: which paragraph applies`

-- (1): the spouse died before 6 April 2016, the survivor was under pensionable age then, and has not remarried.
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `regulation 16(1)`
-- (1)(c): a marriage or civil partnership after the death and before pensionable age takes the survivor out.
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) TRUE) EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`
-- (1)(a): died on 5 April 2016, the last day before the date: in (1) even though the deceased had reached pensionable age.
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 5 4 2016) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `regulation 16(1)`
-- (2): the deceased reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 but died on or after it; the survivor under pensionable age then.
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `regulation 16(2)`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 6 4 2016) (JUST (Date 5 4 2016)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `regulation 16(2)`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) TRUE) EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`
-- (2)(a): the deceased reached pensionable age on 6 April 2016, which is not before it.
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) (JUST (Date 6 4 2016)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`
-- (2)(a): a deceased who never reached pensionable age is not within (2) or (3).
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`
-- (3): the deceased reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 but died on or after it; the survivor was over pensionable age then.
-- No bar on remarriage in (3).
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2016) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `regulation 16(3)`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2016) (Date 1 4 2020) TRUE) EQUALS `regulation 16(3)`
-- Fork F14: the day of reaching pensionable age counts as over it.
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 3 2020) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `regulation 16(3)`
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 28 2 2020) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `regulation 16(2)`
-- Died before 6 April 2016 and the survivor was over pensionable age then: not within (1) or (3).
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2014) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`

§§ `Regulation 16(6): the date for the inherited amount`

#ASSERT `the date for the inherited amount` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2020)
#ASSERT `the date for the inherited amount` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2020)
-- (6)(b): within (3), the date the spouse or civil partner died.
#ASSERT `the date for the inherited amount` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2016) (JUST (Date 1 1 2015)) (Date 1 3 2016) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2016)
#ASSERT `the date for the inherited amount` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 16(4): the inherited amount`

-- Half of the weekly rate.
#ASSERT `the inherited amount` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) 3 EQUALS JUST 1.5
#ASSERT `the inherited amount` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) 7.2 EQUALS JUST 3.6
#ASSERT `the inherited amount` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) TRUE) 3 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 15: entitlement and rate`

-- All of 15(2)(a) to (d): reached pensionable age by the date asked about; the survivor married before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT `a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of a state pension under regulation 15` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE) 3 EQUALS JUST 1.5
-- (a): asked the day before reaching pensionable age; and on the day itself.
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 29 2 2020) FALSE))
#ASSERT `a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of a state pension under regulation 15` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 29 2 2020) FALSE) 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (d): no inherited amount under regulation 16.
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor` (Date 1 6 2014) NOTHING (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 4 2020) TRUE))

`a survivor married on` MEANS GIVEN married YIELD `Facts about a survivor` WITH
    `the date as at which the question is asked` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS TRUE
    `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS TRUE
    `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS married
    `the date the deceased died` IS Date 1 6 2014
    `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS NOTHING
    `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS Date 1 3 2020
    `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS FALSE
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
    `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
    `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE

-- (c): the marriage took place, or the civil partnership was formed, before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT `a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor married on` (Date 5 4 2016))
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor married on` (Date 6 4 2016)))
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor married on` (Date 1 1 2017)))

-- (1) and (b): the deceased paid graduated contributions, and died while married or civil partners.
`a survivor with` MEANS GIVEN paid, married YIELD `Facts about a survivor` WITH
    `the date as at which the question is asked` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS paid
    `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS married
    `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS Date 1 6 2010
    `the date the deceased died` IS Date 1 6 2014
    `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS NOTHING
    `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS Date 1 3 2020
    `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS FALSE
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
    `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
    `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor with` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor with` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 15` (`a survivor with` TRUE FALSE))

§§ `Regulation 17: up-rating`

GIVEN `survivor pension` IS A NUMBER
      others IS A NUMBER
      `full rate` IS A NUMBER
      `new full rate` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      order IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension`
`up-rating facts` `survivor pension` others `full rate` `new full rate` order MEANS
    `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension` WITH
        `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15` IS `survivor pension`
        `the sum of the rates of any state pension the person is entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act` IS others
        `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase` IS `full rate`
        `the full rate of the state pension after an increase, if the full rate is increased` IS `new full rate`
        `the percentage specified in an uprating order, if one comes into force` IS order

`case 3` MEANS `regulation 17(3) and (4): the pension rises by the same percentage as the full rate`
`case 5` MEANS `regulation 17(5) to (7): the pension rises by a percentage of the shortfall, the excess, or both`
`case 8` MEANS `regulation 17(8) and (9): the pension rises by the percentage in the uprating order`

-- Which case: the other pensions alone at or above the full rate (8); below it and with the survivor's pension at or below it (3);
-- below it and with the survivor's pension taking the total over it (5). Full rate 200 throughout.
#ASSERT `the up-rating case that applies` (`up-rating facts` 50 0 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS `case 3`
#ASSERT `the up-rating case that applies` (`up-rating facts` 50 150 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS `case 3`
#ASSERT `the up-rating case that applies` (`up-rating facts` 50 151 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS `case 5`
#ASSERT `the up-rating case that applies` (`up-rating facts` 50 199 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS `case 5`
#ASSERT `the up-rating case that applies` (`up-rating facts` 50 200 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS `case 8`
#ASSERT `the up-rating case that applies` (`up-rating facts` 50 250 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS `case 8`

-- (3), (4): rises by the same percentage as the full rate (200 to 210 is 5%): 50 rises by 2.5.
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 0 200 (JUST 210) NOTHING) EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 150 200 (JUST 210) NOTHING) EQUALS 2.5
-- (3)(b) needs the full rate to be increased: an uprating order alone does nothing in this case.
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 0 200 NOTHING (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 0 200 (JUST 210) (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 0 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15 after the increase` (`up-rating facts` 50 0 200 (JUST 210) NOTHING) EQUALS 52.5

-- (5) to (7): the other pensions are 151, so the shortfall is 49 and the excess is 50 + 151 - 200 = 1.
-- (6): the full rate rises 5%: 5% of the shortfall, 2.45. (7): an uprating order of 4%: 4% of the excess, 0.04.
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 151 200 (JUST 210) NOTHING) EQUALS 2.45
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 151 200 NOTHING (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 0.04
-- "either or both": both together add (fork F15).
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 151 200 (JUST 210) (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 2.49
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 151 200 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS 0
-- Shortfall 40 and excess 10 (others 160): 5% of 40 is 2 and 4% of 10 is 0.4.
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 160 200 (JUST 210) (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 2.4

-- (8), (9): the other pensions at or above the full rate; the survivor's pension rises by the order's percentage: 4% of 50 is 2.
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 200 200 NOTHING (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 250 200 NOTHING (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 2
-- (8)(b) needs an uprating order: a rise in the full rate alone does nothing here.
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 250 200 (JUST 210) NOTHING) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` (`up-rating facts` 50 250 200 (JUST 210) (JUST (4%))) EQUALS 2

§§ `Regulation 18: a choice`

GIVEN deferred IS A BOOLEAN
      died IS A DATE
      `survivor reaches` IS A DATE
      remarried IS A BOOLEAN
      eight IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a survivor`
`a deferring survivor` deferred died `survivor reaches` remarried eight MEANS
    `Facts about a survivor` WITH
        `the date as at which the question is asked` IS Date 1 4 2020
        `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS TRUE
        `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS TRUE
        `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS Date 1 6 2010
        `the date the deceased died` IS died
        `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS NOTHING
        `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS `survivor reaches`
        `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS remarried
        `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS deferred
        `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS FALSE
        `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS deferred
        `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS eight

-- (1): reached pensionable age, spouse died while married, deferred throughout, and either under pensionable age then and not remarried, or over.
#ASSERT `the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` FALSE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) TRUE FALSE))
-- (1)(d)(ii): over pensionable age when the spouse died: remarriage does not matter.
#ASSERT `the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2014) TRUE FALSE)
-- (1)(a): not yet reached pensionable age at the date asked about.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 5 2020) FALSE FALSE))
-- (8): not entitled to a choice under regulation 18 if entitled to one under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `the conditions of regulation 18(1)(a) to (d) are met` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE TRUE)

`lump sum` MEANS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
`pension` MEANS `a state pension under regulation 20`
`not yet` MEANS `nothing yet, because the person can still make a choice`
`unsaid` MEANS `the Regulations do not say, because the choice was made before its period began`

-- (2), (9), (10): what a choice leads to.
#ASSERT `what is paid when the payment chosen is` `a lump sum` EQUALS `lump sum`
#ASSERT `what is paid when the payment chosen is` `a state pension` EQUALS `pension`
-- (5), (11): failing to choose within the period leads to a lump sum.
#ASSERT `what is paid where no choice has been made` TRUE EQUALS `lump sum`
#ASSERT `what is paid where no choice has been made` FALSE EQUALS `not yet`

`a choice of` MEANS GIVEN chosen, manner, specified, made, reasonable, paid, full, currency YIELD `A choice made under regulation 18` WITH
    `the payment chosen` IS chosen
    `how the choice was made` IS `How something was given` WITH
        `the manner` IS manner
        `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it` IS specified
        `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used` IS FALSE
    `the facts for the period` IS `Facts for the period for a choice` WITH
        `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice` IS LIST Date 1 3 2026
        `the date the person claimed a state pension` IS Date 1 1 2026
        `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS Date 1 1 2026
        `the date the choice was made` IS made
    `the facts for a late choice` IS `Facts for a late choice` WITH
        `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS reasonable
        `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS paid
        `it has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS full
        `it has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS currency

GIVEN choice IS A MAYBE `A choice made under regulation 18`
      ended IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for the payment under regulation 18`
`payment facts` choice ended MEANS
    `Facts for the payment under regulation 18` WITH
        `the choice the person made, if any` IS choice
        `the period for making a choice has ended without one being made` IS ended

-- The notice is dated 1 March 2026, so the period is 1 March to 31 May 2026 (regulation 4(2), fork F7).
-- (4): in the period, a choice in writing to a specified office.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a lump sum` `in writing` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) FALSE) EQUALS `lump sum`
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in writing` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) FALSE) EQUALS `pension`
-- (3): a choice not made in the manner of regulation 5(2) and (3) is no choice: nothing yet, or a lump sum once the period has ended.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in some other way` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) FALSE) EQUALS `not yet`
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in writing` FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS `lump sum`
-- (5): no choice and the period has ended: a lump sum; the period still running: nothing yet.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` NOTHING TRUE) EQUALS `lump sum`
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS `not yet`
-- (4), (6): a late choice (after 31 May) for a state pension, allowed: the Secretary of State thinks it reasonable and no lump sum was paid.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in writing` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS `pension`
-- Allowed where a lump sum was paid and has been repaid in full and in the currency.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in writing` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)) TRUE) EQUALS `pension`
-- Not allowed where a lump sum was paid and not repaid: the person stays with the lump sum (5).
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in writing` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)) TRUE) EQUALS `lump sum`
-- Not allowed where the Secretary of State does not consider it reasonable.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in writing` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS `lump sum`
-- A late choice for a lump sum, allowed: a lump sum.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a lump sum` `in writing` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS `lump sum`
-- A choice made before its period begins: the Regulations do not say.
#ASSERT `what is paid under regulation 18` (`payment facts` (JUST (`a choice of` `a state pension` `in writing` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) FALSE) EQUALS `unsaid`

§§ `Regulation 18(7): altering a choice`

-- Paragraph (7)(a): regulation 6(3) applies; 800 lump sum less 500 already paid as a state pension leaves 300.
#ASSERT `the part of the lump sum under regulation 19 still to be paid` 800 `less` 500 EQUALS 300

§§ `Regulation 19: the lump sum`

#ASSERT `the date the person becomes entitled to make a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 3 2020
#ASSERT `the date the person becomes entitled to make a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2014) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 6 2014
#ASSERT `the date the person becomes entitled to make a choice under regulation 18` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 3 2020
#ASSERT `the lump sum payable under regulation 19` 1200 `given` `lump sum` EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `the lump sum payable under regulation 19` 1200 `given` `pension` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the lump sum payable under regulation 19` 1200 `given` `not yet` EQUALS 0

§§ `Regulation 20: a state pension`

-- (1): reached pensionable age; spouse died while married; (c) under and not remarried, or over; (d) the deceased was entitled to
-- an increase, or deferred when died; (e) and (f) only for a person entitled to a choice (or who would be but for (8)).
#ASSERT `a state pension is payable under regulation 20` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE) `given` `pension`
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 20` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE) `given` `lump sum`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 20` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE) `given` `not yet`)
-- (f): not entitled to a choice because (8) applies, but to be paid a state pension by virtue of 18(9)(b) or (10)(b).
#ASSERT `a state pension is payable under regulation 20` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE TRUE) `given` `pension`
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 20` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE TRUE) `given` `lump sum`)
-- (d)(i): the deceased was entitled to an increase (not deferred): no choice, so (e) and (f) do not bite.
`increase only` MEANS `Facts about a survivor` WITH
    `the date as at which the question is asked` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person` IS TRUE
    `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died` IS TRUE
    `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on` IS Date 1 6 2010
    `the date the deceased died` IS Date 1 6 2014
    `the date the deceased reached pensionable age` IS NOTHING
    `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age` IS Date 1 3 2020
    `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age` IS FALSE
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS FALSE
    `the deceased was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS TRUE
    `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the deceased died` IS FALSE
    `the survivor is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `a state pension is payable under regulation 20` `increase only` `given` `not yet`
-- Neither (d)(i) nor (d)(ii): not payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 20` (`a deferring survivor` FALSE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE FALSE) `given` `pension`)
-- (c)(i): remarried before pensionable age: not payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`a state pension is payable under regulation 20` (`a deferring survivor` TRUE (Date 1 6 2014) (Date 1 3 2020) TRUE FALSE) `given` `pension`)

-- (2): half the weekly rate of the increase.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of a state pension under regulation 20` 5 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of a state pension under regulation 20` 0.6 EQUALS 0.3
-- (3): raised by the percentage in an uprating order, at that time: 2.5 rises 4% to 2.6.
#ASSERT `the rate of a state pension under regulation 20 after an uprating order` 2.5 `and the percentage specified in the order being` (4%) EQUALS 2.6
